{"evt":"summary_set","id":"note:note-mqq0vwgsq1k","workspace":"D:\\zonoid","summary":"DECISION (2026-06-22, user-directed): the JUDGING->READY gate becomes STRICT and loses its time-based auto-release. INVARIANT: a node with ANY unjudged autowire candidate edge is NOT READY until those edges are judged (keep/prune) — remove JUDGING_TIMEOUT_MS (soft ~10min, lib/judge.js:~465) and JUDGING_HARD_CEILING_MS (hard ~30min, ~484); the 409 claim gate at routes/overlay.js:466-471 no longer has a timeout exception. RATIONALE: the timeout was only a backstop against the slow/hang-prone ASYNC background judge. Now that judging is fast + synchronous (P1 sync judge-drain reusing runJudgeLoop) and can be driven ON DEMAND via a CLI (node scripts/judge-drain-once.js --node <key>), the timeout is vestigial. The CLI judge REPLACES the timeout as the escape hatch: a gated node is un-gated by actually judging its edges, not by waiting out a clock. SAFETY: no infinite-stuck risk — both the eager judge (auto on node-add) and the CLI (manual) can drain a gated node. This REFINES the JUDGING-gate detail of the floor-drop decision (note-mqq0q02xylw said 'until judged OR timed-out'; the 'or timed-out' branch is now removed). Shipped as feature orch/feature/bench-prod-parity task P6 (codex/p6-strict-judging-gate), gated on P1.","actor":"overlay-sync","ts":"2026-06-23T02:28:46.848Z"}
